    "text": "01 Interpretation A backtest answers a conditional statement: given the imported observations, the selected calendar and universe, the stated strategy document, and the configured execution model, what sequence of decisions and accounting transitions does the engine produce? R = F( D id , S v , E , C , V ) The result is therefore conditional on model structure and data quality. It does not estimate causal effect, establish market predictability, or demonstrate that an order could have been executed at the simulated price and quantity. Interpretive boundary Return, drawdown, Sharpe-like measures and win rates are properties of one historical simulation. They must be read with the tested interval, trial count, costs, universe construction and out-of-sample evidence."
